Joe,

By truncated exponential, if you mean

f(x) = lambda * exp(-lambda * x)/ (1 - exp( -lambda *x ) )

for 0 <= x < 5 and 0 otherwise,

  rexp(n.desired,lambda) %% 5.0  # use memoryless property to advantage

should do the job. 

Chuck

