I meant to add in my previous note that the Alzola/Harrell e-book emphasizes 
three approaches to your problem.  The first is to compare the vector of 
subject IDs to a one-lagged vector of subject IDs.  The Hmisc library has a 
special function Lag which helps in padding with blanks or NAs and with 
processing factor variables.  The second approach is to reshape the strung-out 
data using the Hmisc reShape function.  The third involves direct computation 
of one-number summaries such as the highest blood pressure over time within 
subject.

The Alzola/Harrell e-book also has a comparison of SAS and S which might be 
useful to you.

In my previous note there was a typo: I meant to say "although SAS excels in 
processing huge datasets", instead of "also SAS excels ...".

Frank

