Recently, I asked how to append plots to two different plot windows while 
in a single loop.  I'm grateful to Tony Plate and Bill Dunlap for alerting 
me to dev.xxx commands.

Unfortunately, I still can't do what I want.

Bill suggested using dev.set within the loop to switch between
windows. For instance ...

x<-1:20
dev.start() # this starts graphsheet() on Windows, motif() on Unix
window1 <- dev.cur()
par(mfrow=c(2,2))
dev.start()
window2 <- dev.cur()
par(mfrow=c(2,2))
for(i in 1:4) {
        dev.set(window1)
        plot(x, x+i, main=paste("x vs. x+",i,sep=""))
        dev.set(window2)
        plot(-x, x+i, main=paste("-x vs. x+",i,sep=""))
}

This works fine, unless the number of iterations exceeds the number of 
plots allocated per page by par(mfrow=). For instance ...

x<-1:20
dev.start() # this starts graphsheet() on Windows, motif() on Unix
window1 <- dev.cur()
par(mfrow=c(2,2))
dev.start()
window2 <- dev.cur()
par(mfrow=c(2,2))
for(i in 1:5) {   #INCREASE ITERATIONS TO 5
        dev.set(window1)
        plot(x, x+i, main=paste("x vs. x+",i,sep=""))
        dev.set(window2)
        plot(-x, x+i, main=paste("-x vs. x+",i,sep=""))
}

...obliterates the first four plots in each window.

So I'm afraid my question still stands.

John Thaden

