From jconnor at bio.ri.ccf.org  Wed Jan  9 21:45:09 2002
From: jconnor at bio.ri.ccf.org (Jason Connor)
Date: Wed, 09 Jan 2002 16:45:09 -0500
Subject: Survival analysis update
Message-ID: <Pine.SOL.3.96.1020109164359.9976c-100000@foster>

        
Please disregard the previous post.

I found an error in my datastep work (to use SAS jargon) that led to (a)  
SAS and S-plus producing different results and (b) Surv(start, end, event)
and Surv(end, event) producing different results -- when testing with 
variables that don't differ over time.

Happily, everything agree now.

For those interested, +cluster(studyid) is not necessary since IDs never
provide data at the same time points.  Though a single ID may have
multiple entires, these entries cover different periods of time. 

Thanks to anyone and everyone (Steve McKinney, Terry Therneau, and others)
who gave my problem some thought!

Jason

