1) The first argument to assign() is a character string, not a name, so
assign(goop[i], i + 100, where = 1)

is what you need.

2) You seem to want to assign to the working directory, which is where=1
not frame=0 (and why abbreviate: it makes life difficult for your
readers).  You can assign to frame=0 (or where=0) and this will be visible
from functions you run, but not from the command line.

3) All S functions return something, so include invisible() at the end if
you don't want surprises.

I won't try to explain frames and the search path here: see the Blue Book
or `S Programming'.

