From jjthaden at flash.net  Sat Jan 12 03:23:20 2002
From: jjthaden at flash.net (John Thaden)
Date: Fri, 11 Jan 2002 21:23:20 -0600
Subject: SUMMARY: Generating two multi-page graphsheets in a loop
Message-ID: <5.1.0.14.0.20020111210325.00a8d978@pop.flash.net>

Thanks for the abundant replies to my question, reproduced below.  Karen 
Byron drew my attention to the pages argument of graphsheet, which when set 
to "every graph" gives the desired result.  Here is Karen's code:

x <- 1:20
graphsheet(pages = "every graph")
window1 <- dev.cur()
par(mfrow = c(2, 2))
graphsheet(pages = "every graph")
window2 <- dev.cur()
par(mfrow = c(2, 2))
for(i in 1:5) {
dev.set(window1)
plot(x, x + i, main=paste("x vs. x+", i, sep=""))
dev.set(window2)
plot(-x, x + i, main=paste("-x vs. x+", i, sep=""))
}

With pages="every graph", the fifth plot no longer overwrites the 
first.  Alternatively, the "every graph" setting can be GUI-specified, at 
options|graph options|auto pages.

Thanks again, all.

