Hello,

Using S+ 2000, R3 on Win98.

I have a minor puzzle dealing with how to incorporate the loop increment
into a vector name for a vector created inside of a loop.  As a toy example,
suppose I have a simple loop construct and want to define a numeric vector.

b <- 5
for (j in 1:b){
        tmp.j <- numeric(b)  # or say a series of calculations
}

If I look for one of the vectors, tmp.1, it does not exist
> tmp.1
Error: Object "tmp.1" not found

If I look for tmp.j, it exists as a numeric vector of length 5.
> tmp.j
[1] 0 0 0 0 0

I have explored some constructs involving things like
as.name(paste("tmp",j,sep=".")) and have failed to arrive at anything which
provides named objects incorporating the increment value.  Any suggestions
(other than to not use loops) as to coding options or subject material ?
I'll summarize for the group unless the answer is embarrassingly trivial.

Thanks in advance,

Peter Scherer
Dow AgroSciences
Indianapolis, IN

