In-Reply-To: <4.2.0.58.20020122110759.00b25550@uio-pop.uio.no>
References: <4.2.0.58.20020122110759.00b25550@uio-pop.uio.no>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.31.0201221102340.1172-100000@gannet.stats>

On Tue, 22 Jan 2002, [iso-8859-1] Torbjørn Ergon wrote:

>
> According to
>
> Burnham, K.P., Anderson, D.R., 1998. Model selection and inference: a
> practical information-theoretic approach. New-York, Springer-Verlag, 353 p.
>
> model selection based on AIC tends to select overparameterized models when
> the ratio K/n is high (K= no. parameters, n = sample size), and they
> recommend using
>
> AICc = - 2 * log(maximized likelihood) + 2 * K * (n / (n - K - 1)
>
> Does anybody have a modified version of stepAIC (MASS library) that uses
> AICc as the criterion? (one cannot do this by changing the k argument to
> stepAIC because the scale of the penalty in AICc depends on K).

Well, k = 2*n/(n-K-1), so for a modest range of K you *can* change k.
Also, k is never used by stepAIC, only by extractAIC, so it would be
trivial to modify the extractAIC methods you are interested in (if n is
available in the fitted object, that is).

