On Tue, 22 Jan 2002 Pierre.Ilouga at evotecoai.com wrote:

> Dear Splus user,
> it could be possible that I'm doing something wrong.

Using names as indexing element is subject to partial matching,
whereas using match (which is what underlies is.element) is not.
Check out the differences between match, charmatch and pmatch.

You are right that if nm is a character vector then x[nm] is potentially
dangerous.  It is better to use x[match(nm, names(x))]

Incidentally, R is different and does not partially match (not that
should be seen as a virtue).

