From puschner at psyres-stuttgart.de  Wed Jan 23 15:11:56 2002
From: puschner at psyres-stuttgart.de (Bernd Puschner)
Date: Wed, 23 Jan 2002 16:11:56 +0100
Subject: summary boxplot with mean
Message-ID: <3C4ED2BC.CFF35827@psyres-stuttgart.de>

thanks to renaud lancelot, bill pikounis, bert gunter and greg snow for
their very helpful answers. there seem to be two solutions with some
variations on the 2nd.

bernd

 ### data = kosther, y=costs, x = therapy

### 1
bwplot(therapy~costs, data=na.omit(kosther), xlab="Kosten (?)",
  key = list(space = "right",
             text = list(c("Mean", "Median")),
             points = list(pch = c(8, 16))),
  panel = function(x, y){
    panel.bwplot(x, y)
    Y <- unique(y)
    for(i in seq(along = Y)){
      X <- x[y == Y[i]]
      points(mean(X), Y[i], pch = 8)
                }
      })

### 2
attach(na.omit(kosther))
sizelist <- split(costs,therapy)
centers <- boxplot(sizelist,style.bxp="att",medpch="-",
                        ylab="Kosten (?)")
points(centers,unlist(lapply(sizelist,mean)),pch="x")

