I programmed this recently - I THINK it's right, but haven't worked with it
a lot (I'm not a statistician or a programmer!). I'd be interested to hear
of any other feedback you get. 
jane

nagelr2<-function(mod,nullmod){
#mod is fitted model
#nullmod is the null model fitted to the same data ie glm(sp~1,)
#written by Jane Elith (j.elith at botany.unimelb.edu.au)
llnull<-sum(log(dbinom(nullmod$y,1,nullmod$fitted.values)))
llfit<-sum(log(dbinom(mod$y,1,mod$fitted.values)))
n<-length(mod$y)
LR<- -2*llnull - -2*llfit
L0<- -2*llnull
nagel<- (1-exp(-LR/n))/(1-exp(-L0/n))
return(nagel)
}

-- FEH, Jr ----

This is builtin to the Design library, if you are using binary or orginal 
logistic or a survival model.  -Frank Harrell

