Yes. This happens on Windows 9x with an HP printer driver installed. Ask
your technical support for the bugfix patch, which works fine (although for
me the instructions were wrong: the easier way to make sure a library is
always attached it to use an S.init file in S_HOME\local).

HP wrote its printer drivers incorrectly to reset the FPU controls.
Lots of applications have suffered from that, although usually immediately
after printing.

