Subject: Summary: : random sample within reps accounting for NAs
Message-ID: <24E34B7B296AD411815300805F578D94B428A1@elnte4.nam.dow.com>

Thanks to all who responded to my sampling query.  Suggestions and
alternative approaches were given by Andy Liaw, Gregory Warnes, Jingshan
Zhang, James Rizopoulos, Eric Elguero and Peter Anthoni.  The most
transparent code was provided by Greg Warnes and Jingshan Zhang and is
provided below.  Thanks again to all of you for providing a collection of
ways to approach this problem.

# Greg Warnes
> # the test data
> orig.df
        yield replic trtNo 
 1 -0.5958798      1     1
 2 -0.9305458      2     1
 3 -0.5504828      1     2
 4 -2.5729802      2     2
 5  1.3542354      1     3
 6  1.4630517      2     3
 7         NA      1     4
 8  0.4343464      2     4
 9  1.7139252      1     5
10 -0.5081621      2     5

# get rid of missing values
nomiss <- na.omit(orig.df)
# get the row names in groups by treatment
rnames <- split( row.names(nomiss), nomiss$trtNo )
# sample 1 row name from each group
snames <- sapply( rnames,  sample, size=1 )
# use the row names to get the randomly selected observations
nomiss[snames,]
        yield replic trtNo 
 1 -0.5958798      1     1
 4 -2.5729802      2     2
 6  1.4630517      2     3
 8  0.4343464      2     4
10 -0.5081621      2     5

# jingshan zhang
#Hello, Peter: According to your description, I would like 
#to list some facts which I am not 100% sure.
#1) Row 2*k-1 and Row 2*k are bound together, in the sense
#   that one and only one of them will be selected.
#2) If a pair contains one NA, then the other non-NA observation
#   will definitely be chosen. Be sure thare is no pair that both
#   observation are NAs.
RowNA<-which(is.na(orig.df)) #which rows contain NA.
m<-dim(orig.df)[1]/2   # m pairs of observations
Select<-rep(T,2*m)  #Each element indicates whether the corresponding row
                    # will be selected or not.
Select[RowNA]<-F    # Won't select these NA rows.
PairwoNA<-setdiff(1:m,ifelse(RowNA%/%2==0,RowNA/2,(RowNA+1)/2)) 
                    # Which pair doesn't include NA from pair 1 to pair m.
RanReplic<-rbinom(length(PairwoNA),1,.5) # T means the first observation
  # within that pair will not be selected.
Select[ifelse(RanReplic==1,2*PairwoNA-1,2*PairwoNA)]<-F
orig.df[Select,]

Peter Scherer
Dow AgroSciences
Indianapolis, IN

