Subject: Summary of Responses -- Trouble Linking Fortran subroutines
Message-ID: <3C517219.7000500@stanford.edu>

For your information, the description of my problem is shown below.

I greatly appreciate the quick assistance of Chuck Taylor, Brian Ripley, 
David Smith, Matt Calder and Ravi Varadhan. Thanks.

Chuck Taylor pointed out that Splus interfacing with C and Fortran is 
discussed in Chapter 15 of the Programmer's Guide.  Having looked 
through the indices of the various manuals, I had missed this because 
"Fortran" was not listed in the index.  (Chuck indicated that this 
omission has been corrected.)

Brian Ripley indicated that using Fortran was tricky and especially 
problematic when the Fortran code makes calls to functions in the 
sqpe.dll or uses character variables.  He also allerted me to the useful 
document "Complements for 'S Programing'" which can be found starting at 
http://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/pub/MASS3/Sprog. The document provides updates 
regarding linking under S+6.

Matt Calder saved the day by sending me an example using the Fortran 90 
compiler Microsoft PowerStation.  The problem I had was that the DLL 
created using Microsoft Developer Studio in the standard way did not 
create an export name for the subroutine that Splus recognized. 
Following Matt's example, when I added the line of code

MS$ATTRIBUTES DLLEXPORT, ALIAS:'subroutine_name' :: subroutine_name

to the subroutine Splus called, things worked correctly.

Again, thanks.

Hamp

