As far as I know there is no such operator, but here is a function that
almost does what you want:

---(cut here)---
powerSet <- function(x) {
        if(length(x) == 0)
                return(vector(mode(x), 0))
        x <- sort(unique(x))
        K <- NULL
        for(m in x)
                K <- rbind(cbind(K, F), cbind(K, T))
        apply(K, 1, function(x, s) s[x], s = x)
}
---(cut here)---

Test:

> powerSet(LETTERS[1:3])
[[1]]:
[1] "A"

[[2]]:
[1] "B"

[[3]]:
[1] "A" "B"

[[4]]:
[1] "C"

[[5]]:
[1] "A" "C"

[[6]]:
[1] "B" "C"

[[7]]:
[1] "A" "B" "C"

If the set itself is null the value is a null vector of that mode.

I say "almost" because the ordering is not quite what you had in your
example.  If this is a problem, fixing it is a minor exercise for the reader
with a one-line solution.

Bill Venables.

