From verkerk at candiensten.nl  Wed Jan 30 12:09:23 2002
From: verkerk at candiensten.nl (Dick Verkerk)
Date: Wed, 30 Jan 2002 13:09:23 +0100
Subject: "Quantitative Financial Risk Management" by Dr. Alexander McNeil
Message-ID: <3C57E273.AF61D331@candiensten.nl>

Dear S-PLUS User,

Are you interested in Extreme Value Theory (EVT), Advanced Market 
Risk Models, Financial Time Series and Volatility or, more in 
general, in Quantitative Financial Risk Management? 

We are most pleased to present to you the special two-day course 
"Quantitative Financial Risk Management" by Dr. Alexander McNeil on 
March 7-8 in Amsterdam.

Dr. Alexander McNeil, of the ETH (Swiss Federal Technical University) 
in Zurich, is an internationally recognized authority in this field 
and author of the extreme value analysis software (EVIS) written in 
S-PLUS.
http://www.math.ethz.ch/~mcneil/software.html

The course aims to provide risk managers with a better understanding 
of quantitative tools for modern financial risk management.  Whenever 
appropriate, theory will be illustrated by practical examples developed 
in the powerful S-PLUS environment, although prior familiarity with 
S-PLUS will not be assumed and the course may be followed by non-users 
of S-PLUS. 

The central technical issues are volatility, extremes, correlation, 
and the advanced statistical methods required to model these 
phenomena. Financial risk management confronts us with a real world 
of heavy-tailed risks, rapid changes and complex interdependencies 
which force us to go beyond standard statistical models and 
simplifying assumptions of normality to develop more sophisticated 
methodology.

More information on the content of the course can be found at:
